2. Augmented State Space and Dynamics

2.1 State Vector

Let $R$ denote the finite index set of critical resources, $|R|$ its cardinality, and $\mathcal{F}_C$ the set of critical civilizational functions
\mathcal{F}_C = \{\text{Energy}, \text{Water}, \text{Atmosphere}, \text{Food}, \text{Habitat}, \text{Maintenance}, \text{Manufacturing}, \text{Health}, \text{Information}, \text{Transport}\}.


The augmented state of the Martian node $v_M$ is
z_M(t) = \begin{bmatrix} x_M(t) \\ S_M(t) \\ C_{M,\mathrm{local}}(t) \end{bmatrix} \in \mathcal{Z}_M = \mathcal{X}_M \times \mathbb{R}_+^{|R|} \times \mathbb{R}_+^{|R|} \subset \mathbb{R}^N,


where $N = n_x + 2|R|$, $x_M \in \mathcal{X}_M \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{n_x}$ denotes industrial capital, $S_M(r,t) \in \mathbb{R}_+$ denotes the physical stock of resource $r \in R$, and $C_{M,\mathrm{local}}(r,t) \in \mathbb{R}_+$ denotes local production or regeneration capacity for $r$.

2.2 Dynamics

The evolution is governed by
\begin{aligned}
\dot{x}_M(t) &= f_x\bigl(z_M(t), \pi(z_M(t)), d(t)\bigr), \\
\dot{S}_M(r,t) &= -N_{\mathrm{requis}}(r,t) + C_{M,\mathrm{local}}(r,t) + \rho_M(r,z_M(t),t), \\
\dot{C}_{M,\mathrm{local}}(r,t) &= \Phi_r\bigl(z_M(t), \pi(z_M(t)), d(t)\bigr),
\end{aligned}
\tag{2.1}


where $\pi \in \mathcal{U}_M$ is the local feedback policy, $d \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$ is an admissible perturbation, $N_{\mathrm{requis}}(r,t) > 0$ is the nominal requirement rate, and $\rho_M$ is a recycling term.

Assumption 2.1 (Regularity). The vector field $F: \mathcal{Z}_M \times \mathcal{U}_M \times \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}} \to \mathbb{R}^N$ defining (2.1) is locally Lipschitz in $z_M$ and continuous on $\mathcal{U}_M \times \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$.

Under Assumption 2.1 and Carathéodory conditions on $(u,d)$, (2.1) admits a unique maximal solution $z_M(\cdot; z_0, u, d)$ for each admissible pair.

2.3 Perturbation Classes

The perturbation index set is
\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{pert}} = \{P, I, A, H, K\},


corresponding to Physical, Informational, Algorithmic, Human/Institutional, and Kinetic/Orbital disturbances. The admissible perturbation set is
\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}} = \left\{ d = (d_P, d_I, d_A, d_H, d_K) \;\middle|\; \|d_i\| \le \Delta_i,\ i \in \mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{pert}} \right\}.
\tag{2.2}


Compactness of $\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$ is immediate from (2.2).

2.4 Hybrid Reclassification

A flow initially non-critical may become critical under degradation. To model this rigorously, we equip $\mathcal{Z}_M$ with a hybrid automaton structure with discrete modes $\sigma \in \{\text{nominal}, \text{reclassified}\}$:
\dot{z}_M(t) = F_\sigma\bigl(z_M(t), \pi(z_M(t)), d(t)\bigr).


The switching surface is
\mathcal{S} = \left\{ z_M \in \mathcal{Z}_M \;\middle|\; \exists r \in R_j^{\mathrm{ess}},\ C_{M,\mathrm{local}}(r) + \frac{\tilde{S}_M(r)}{T_{\mathrm{rec}}(r)} < N_{\mathrm{requis}}(r) \text{ under } u^{\mathrm{non-crit}} \text{ alone} \right\}.


Across $\mathcal{S}$, the state is assumed continuous:
z_M(t^+) = z_M(t^-), \quad \forall t \text{ with } z_M(t) \in \mathcal{S}.
\tag{2.3}


This reflects the physical fact that capital, stocks, and production capacities do not jump. Only the vector field $F_\sigma$ may switch. The hybrid barrier condition, when required, is
h_{\mathrm{via}}^+(z_M^+) \ge h_{\mathrm{via}}^+(z_M^-), \quad \forall z_M \in \mathcal{S}.

