4. Barrier Functions and Viability Domains

4.1 Composite Viability Barrier

We resolve the circularity between the viability domain and the barrier function by defining a single composite barrier:
h_{\mathrm{via}}^+(z_M) = \min\bigl( h_{\mathrm{via}}(z_M),\; \delta_{\mathrm{crit}} - \mathcal{D}(z_M) \bigr).
\tag{4.1}


The viable domain is the zero-superlevel set
\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{viable}}^+ = \left\{ z_M \in \mathcal{Z}_M \;\middle|\; h_{\mathrm{via}}^+(z_M) \ge 0 \right\}.

Proposition 4.1. $\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{viable}}^+ = \{z_M : h_{\mathrm{via}}(z_M) \ge 0\} \cap \{z_M : \mathcal{D}(z_M) \le \delta_{\mathrm{crit}}\}$.

Proof. Since $\min(a,b) \ge 0 \iff a \ge 0 \land b \ge 0$. $\square$

Under Assumptions 2.1 and 3.1, $h_{\mathrm{via}}^+$ is continuous if $h_{\mathrm{via}}$ is continuous and $\mathcal{D}$ is continuous in $z_M$. Differentiability follows from the differentiability of $h_{\mathrm{via}}$ and $\mathcal{D}$ except on the measure-zero set where $h_{\mathrm{via}}(z_M) = \delta_{\mathrm{crit}} - \mathcal{D}(z_M)$; under (A6) below we exclude this degeneracy on the boundary.

4.2 Non-circular Recoverability Barrier

Let $\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+ \subset \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{viable}}^+$ be a designated nominal domain with non-empty interior. The recoverability barrier is defined intrinsically, via the differential game of reachability to $\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+$:
h_{\mathrm{rec}}(z_M) = \tau_{\max} - \min\left( \inf_{\pi \in \mathcal{U}_M} \sup_{d \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}} \inf\left\{ T \ge 0 \;\middle|\; z_M(T; z_M, \pi, d) \in \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+ \right\},\; \tau_{\max} + \kappa \right),
\tag{4.2}


where $\tau_{\max} > 0$ is the maximal acceptable reconstruction time and $\kappa > 0$ is a regularization constant.

Proposition 4.2 (Boundedness). $h_{\mathrm{rec}}(z_M) \in [-\kappa, \tau_{\max}]$ for all $z_M \in \mathcal{Z}_M$.

Proof. The inner infimum is bounded below by $0$ and above by $\tau_{\max} + \kappa$ by truncation. Subtracting from $\tau_{\max}$ yields the stated range. $\square$

Crucially, (4.2) does not reference $\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{recoverable}}^+$, eliminating the circularity of earlier formulations.

Definition 4.3 (Recoverable domain).
\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{recoverable}}^+ = \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{viable}}^+ \cap \left\{ z_M \;\middle|\; h_{\mathrm{rec}}(z_M) \ge 0 \right\}.

4.3 Nested Structure

Proposition 4.4. $\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+ \subseteq \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{recoverable}}^+ \subseteq \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{viable}}^+$.

Proof. The second inclusion is Definition 4.3. For the first: if $z_M \in \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+$, then the inner infimum in (4.2) is $0$, so $h_{\mathrm{rec}}(z_M) = \tau_{\max} \ge 0$. Also $\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+ \subseteq \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{viable}}^+$ by hypothesis. $\square$

