Appendix B. Properties of the Leontief Bottleneck Metric

B.1 Elementary Properties

Proposition B.1. Let $\mathcal{D} : \mathcal{Z}_M \to [0,1]$ be defined by (3.1). Then:

(i) Range. For all $z \in \mathcal{Z}_M$, $\mathcal{D}(z) \in [0,1]$.

(ii) Monotonicity in buffers. For fixed $(x_M, C_{M,\mathrm{local}})$, $\mathcal{D}$ is non-increasing in $\tilde{S}_M$: if $\tilde{S}_M^1 \leq \tilde{S}_M^2$ componentwise, then $\mathcal{D}(x_M, \tilde{S}_M^1, C_{M,\mathrm{local}}) \geq \mathcal{D}(x_M, \tilde{S}_M^2, C_{M,\mathrm{local}})$.

(iii) Monotonicity in capacity. For fixed $(x_M, \tilde{S}_M)$, $\mathcal{D}$ is non-increasing in $C_{M,\mathrm{local}}$.

(iv) Vanishing. $\mathcal{D}(z) = 0$ iff for all $j \in \mathcal{F}_C$ and all $r \in R_j^{\mathrm{ess}}$, $C_{M,\mathrm{local}}(r) + \tilde{S}_M(r)/T_{\mathrm{rec}}(r) \geq N_{\mathrm{requis}}(r)$.

Proof. (i) The positive part is by construction nonnegative; the ratio inside the parentheses is at least $1 - (\cdot)/N_{\mathrm{requis}}$, and since $C_{M,\mathrm{local}}, \tilde{S}_M \geq 0$, the ratio $\geq 0$, hence the positive part $\leq 1$. (ii) and (iii) follow from monotonicity of $r \mapsto (1-r)_+$. (iv) $\max_j \max_r (\cdot)_+ = 0$ iff each $(\cdot)_+ = 0$ iff each argument $\leq 0$. $\square$

B.2 Lipschitz Continuity

Proposition B.2. Assume $C_{M,\mathrm{local}}, \tilde{S}_M, N_{\mathrm{requis}}$ are locally Lipschitz in $z$ with modulus $L$, and $N_{\mathrm{requis}}(r,t) \geq n_{\min} > 0$ uniformly. Then $\mathcal{D}$ is locally Lipschitz.

Proof. The maps $z \mapsto C_{M,\mathrm{local}}(r) + \tilde{S}_M(r)/T_{\mathrm{rec}}(r)$ and $z \mapsto N_{\mathrm{requis}}(r)$ are locally Lipschitz. Division by $N_{\mathrm{requis}} \geq n_{\min}$ preserves local Lipschitzness. The positive-part operator $(\cdot)_+$ is $1$-Lipschitz. The max of finitely many Lipschitz functions is Lipschitz with the same modulus. Composition preserves the property. $\square$

B.3 Growth Bound

Lemma B.3. If $N_{\mathrm{requis}}(r,t) \geq n_{\min} > 0$ and $\mathcal{D}(z_M(t_0)) \leq \delta < \delta_{\mathrm{crit}}$, then for small $\varepsilon > 0$,
\mathcal{D}(z_M(t_0 + \varepsilon)) \leq \delta + L_f \varepsilon,


where $L_f$ is the local Lipschitz modulus of $\mathcal{D} \circ z_M$.

Proof. Direct from Proposition B.2 and the mean value inequality. $\square$

