Appendix F. Classical Nagumo–Aubin Theorem

Theorem F.1 (Nagumo 1942; Aubin 1991). Let $K \subseteq \mathbb{R}^N$ be closed, and let $F : \mathbb{R}^N \to \mathbb{R}^N$ be locally Lipschitz. Then for every $z_0 \in K$, the unique maximal solution $z(\cdot; z_0)$ satisfies $z(t; z_0) \in K$ for all $t \geq 0$ if and only if
F(z) \in \mathcal{T}_K(z) \quad \forall z \in \partial K.

Theorem F.2 (Robust version). Let $\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^p$ be compact, and let $F : \mathbb{R}^N \times \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}} \to \mathbb{R}^N$ be locally Lipschitz in $z$ uniformly in $d$. Then for every $z_0 \in K$ and every measurable $d : [0,\infty) \to \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$, the unique maximal solution of $\dot{z} = F(z, d(t))$, $z(0) = z_0$, satisfies $z(t) \in K$ for all $t \geq 0$ if and only if
F(z, d) \in \mathcal{T}_K(z) \quad \forall z \in \partial K,\ \forall d \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}.

Proof. Sufficiency follows from applying Nagumo–Aubin to the augmented system $\dot{(z, d)} = (F(z, d), 0)$ with $K \times \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$. Necessity follows from Nagumo–Aubin applied to each constant $d$. $\square$

