Appendix H. Recoverability and the Differential Game

H.1 Well-Posedness of $h_{\mathrm{rec}}$

Lemma H.1. Under (A₁)–(A₃), the map
(z, \pi) \mapsto \sup_{d \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}} \inf\{T \geq 0 : z_M(T; z, \pi, d) \in \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+\}


is well-defined in $[0,\infty]$.

Proof. For fixed $(z, \pi, d)$, the set of hitting times is non-empty (it contains $\infty$ as the infimum of an empty set) and bounded below by $0$. The supremum over compact $\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$ is therefore well-defined in $[0,\infty]$. $\square$

H.2 Boundedness of the Recoverability Barrier

Proposition H.2 (= Proposition 4.2). $h_{\mathrm{rec}}(z) \in [-\kappa, \tau_{\max}]$ for all $z$.

Proof. Let $\Theta(z) := \inf_\pi \sup_d \inf\{T : z_M(T) \in \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+\} \in [0,\infty]$. Then
\min(\Theta(z), \tau_{\max} + \kappa) \in [0, \tau_{\max} + \kappa],


so
h_{\mathrm{rec}}(z) = \tau_{\max} - \min(\Theta(z), \tau_{\max} + \kappa) \in [\tau_{\max} - (\tau_{\max}+\kappa), \tau_{\max} - 0] = [-\kappa, \tau_{\max}]. \ \square

H.3 Sufficiency of Positive $h_{\mathrm{rec}}$

Proposition H.3. If $h_{\mathrm{rec}}(z) \geq 0$, then the inf-sup value satisfies $\Theta(z) \leq \tau_{\max}$, and the corresponding policy $\pi^*$ (if attained) guarantees $\mathcal{R}_c^{\mathrm{robust}}(\tau_{\max}) = 1$.

Proof. $h_{\mathrm{rec}}(z) \geq 0$ means $\tau_{\max} - \min(\Theta(z), \tau_{\max} + \kappa) \geq 0$, i.e., $\min(\Theta(z), \tau_{\max}+\kappa) \leq \tau_{\max}$, which is equivalent to $\Theta(z) \leq \tau_{\max}$. If the infimum over $\pi$ is attained at $\pi^*$, then for every $d \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$,
\inf\{T : z_M(T; z, \pi^*, d) \in \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+\} \leq \Theta(z) \leq \tau_{\max},


so $z_M$ reaches $\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+$ within time $\tau_{\max}$. $\square$

H.4 Non-Circularity

Lemma H.4. $h_{\mathrm{rec}}$ is defined solely in terms of $\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+$ and the dynamics. It does not reference $\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{recoverable}}^+$.

Proof. By inspection of (4.2). $\square$

Corollary H.5. Definition 4.3 of $\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{recoverable}}^+$ is non-circular.

H.5 Stochastic Extension

Theorem H.6. Let $\mathbb{P}_{\mathcal{D}}$ be a probability measure on the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of $\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$-valued trajectories. If $\mathcal{R}_c^{\mathrm{robust}}(\tau^*) = 1$, then $\mathcal{R}_c^{\mathrm{stoch}}(\tau^*) = 1$.

Proof. For every trajectory $d(\cdot) \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$, the hitting time $\inf\{t : z_M(t) \in \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{nominal}}^+\} \leq \tau^*$. Hence the event $\{\inf\{t : \cdots\} \leq \tau^*\}$ is $\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}$-everywhere true, and thus has $\mathbb{P}_{\mathcal{D}}$-probability $1$. $\square$

