Appendix J. Formal Verification Details

J.1 Representation of the State Space

The state space $\mathcal{Z}_M$ is represented as StateSpace := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (TotalDim n_x n_S n_C)). This gives:

· A NormedAddCommGroup, NormedSpace ℝ, and InnerProductSpace ℝ structure;
· Compatible FDeriv and gradient operators from Mathlib;
· Non-degeneracy via [NeZero (TotalDim ...)], ensuring Fin (TotalDim ...) is inhabited.

J.2 Representation of the Barrier

The barrier $h : \mathcal{Z}_M \to \mathbb{R}$ is a real-valued function on the state space. Its gradient gradient h z is defined by Mathlib as the unique vector satisfying
\langle \text{gradient } h\ z, v \rangle = (\text{fderiv } h\ z)\ v


for all $v$.

J.3 The Class-$\mathcal{K}_\infty$ Structure

The structure ClassKInf requires:

· α : ℝ → ℝ
· mono : StrictMonoOn α (Set.Ici 0)
· zero : α 0 = 0
· tendsto : Filter.Tendsto α Filter.atTop Filter.atTop

This captures the classical definition of class-$\mathcal{K}_\infty$ functions, with strict monotonicity on $[0,\infty)$ and divergence at $+\infty$.

J.4 Formalization of Global CBF and Robust Nagumo–Aubin

The predicates are formalized as follows:

```lean
def RobustNagumoAubin (π : StateSpace → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)) : Prop :=
  ∀ z ∈ ∂K, π z ∈ U ∧ ∀ d ∈ D, F z (π z) d ∈ HalfSpaceCone z

def GlobalCBF (π : StateSpace → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)) (α : ClassKInf) : Prop :=
  ∀ z ∈ K, π z ∈ U ∧ ∀ d ∈ D,
    ⟪gradient h z, F z (π z) d⟫_ℝ ≥ - α.α (h z)
```

J.5 The Main Lemma

The key formalized lemma is global_cbf_implies_robust_nagumo:

```lean
theorem global_cbf_implies_robust_nagumo
    (π : StateSpace → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)) (α : ClassKInf)
    (hG : GlobalCBF π α) : RobustNagumoAubin π := by
  intro z hz
  have hz0 : h z = 0 := by simpa [∂K] using hz
  have hzK : z ∈ K := by simp only [K, Set.mem_setOf_eq]; rw [hz0]; exact le_refl 0
  obtain ⟨hU, hD⟩ := hG z hzK
  refine ⟨hU, ?_⟩
  intro d hd
  have hineq := hD d hd
  have heval : - α.α (h z) = 0 := boundary_rhs_zero α hz
  show ⟪gradient h z, F z (π z) d⟫_ℝ ≥ 0
  rw [← heval]; exact hineq
```

J.6 Verified Claims

The module verifies:

· boundary_rhs_zero: On $\partial K$, $h(z) = 0$, so $\alpha(h(z)) = \alpha(0) = 0$.
· global_cbf_implies_robust_nagumo: The main implication $(1) \implies (2)$.

The reverse direction, $(2) \iff (3)$, is definitional under (A₆) and is subsumed by the HalfSpaceCone definition; an explicit statement would be tautological and is therefore omitted.

J.7 Complexity of the Formalization

· Lines of code: Approximately 80, excluding imports.
· Dependencies: Mathlib PiL2, FDeriv.Basic, Gradient, Topology.Basic, Order.Filter.Basic.
· Compilation: Verified under Lean 4 with a current Mathlib snapshot.

J.8 Extensions

The formalization can be extended to:

· The composite barrier $h_{\mathrm{via}}^+ = \min(h_{\mathrm{via}}, \delta_{\mathrm{crit}} - \mathcal{D})$, once $\mathcal{D}$ is formalized.
· The recoverability barrier $h_{\mathrm{rec}}$, requiring a formalization of differential games and reachability.
· The hybrid setting, requiring the Mathlib hybrid systems framework (currently under development).

