Appendix K. Equivalent Formulations and Alternative Approaches

K.1 Viscosity Solutions of Hamilton–Jacobi Equations

The CBF approach can be recast via the Hamilton–Jacobi–Isaacs (HJI) equation:
\min_{d \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}} \max_{u \in \mathcal{U}_M} \langle \nabla h_{\mathrm{via}}^+(z), F(z,u,d) \rangle + \alpha(h_{\mathrm{via}}^+(z)) = 0.


If a viscosity solution exists and is $\mathcal{C}^1$, the two approaches coincide.

K.2 Augmented Barrier with Input Constraints

For systems where $\mathcal{U}_M$ is not a full-dimensional subset of $\mathbb{R}^m$, the CBF condition should be stated as
\exists u \in \mathcal{U}_M : \langle \nabla h_{\mathrm{via}}^+(z), F(z,u,d) \rangle \geq -\alpha(h_{\mathrm{via}}^+(z)) \quad \forall d \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}.


This existential form is often easier to check computationally.

K.3 Set-Theoretic Reformulation

The robust Nagumo–Aubin condition is equivalent to
F(z, \pi(z), \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}) \subseteq \mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{viable}}^+}(z) \quad \forall z \in \partial \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{viable}}^+.


Under (A₆), this is further equivalent to
\min_{d \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{pt}}^{\mathrm{adm}}} \langle \nabla h_{\mathrm{via}}^+(z), F(z, \pi(z), d) \rangle \geq 0 \quad \forall z \in \partial \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{viable}}^+.


Both are useful for algorithmic implementations.

